<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pakhal Lake</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1213</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pakhal Lake is a large artificial lake in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warangal">Warangal</a> region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telangana">Telangana</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, created in 1213 during the reign of the Kakatiya king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganapati-kakatiya">Ganapatideva</a>. Like the nearby Ramappa lake, it was built by damming streams to irrigate the surrounding farmland, part of an extensive Kakatiya system of tanks. It is now surrounded by a wildlife sanctuary.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pakhal-lake.jpg" alt="Pakhal Lake" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alosh Bennett · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pakhal_Lake_Telangana.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
